    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/7/0/70866.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 51,
    "turn_text": "So the fact that the House Freedom Caucus wound up spinning off from the Republican Study Committee spoke to this dynamic you had within the Republican Party, really from 2010 to 2016, in which we read and in my case we wrote ad nauseam about the Republican Civil War and a lot of the ideological brinksmanship that was occurring within the Republican Party. And it seems as though Donald Trump's first his nomination as the Republican presidential nominee, but then his general election victory has, for all intents and purposes, sort of squashed those old ideological beasts within the Republican Party. And now, rather than conservative versus moderate or tea party versus establishment, the divide within the Republican Party today seems to be Trump or never Trump. Are you with the president or are you not with the president? Is that fair",
