    "turn_text": "Look, anybody who talks to the president wants to talk to him not just about the things that are happening today, but about the things that we want to do tomorrow. And he might want to do it this way. And if we want to do it a different way, we start talking through how to get to the same place. And we've been able to do that well. If you look at trade, of the We'll drop all of our tariffs if you drop yours. He doesn't want tariffs, but you noticed a lot of the European countries said, wait a minute, we want to keep our tariffs. You just drop yours. It was a one-sided deal with a lot of countries, and we had been taken advantage of, even by friends of ours. At some point it's not healthy for any relationship if one friend is doing all the work and the other is just taking and so he's I think equalizing a lot of that But he but we talked through what is the endgame and I think it's important to know if he's doing something that maybe we would do differently Why is he doing it? And he's explained it well. I think he's he's been really good at trying to be very up front about us with the strategies that he's using. And frankly, it's hard to argue with the results. The results are actually working for",
